      ]
    },
    {
      "content": "leanprover-community/lint-style-action in `check` mode runs credfeto/action-no-ignored-files, which pipes `git ls-files` through `git check-ignore --stdin -v --no-index` and fails on ANY output. With -v, check-ignore also prints matches of NEGATION patterns (`!path`), so a repo that deliberately keeps some otherwise-ignored files tracked via `!` rules (or force-adds files under an ignored directory) is permanently red. The action also wipes the workspace and rebuilds lint-style with use-mathlib-cache: false, and publishes no tags (pin by SHA). Running `lake exe lint-style` directly as a step after lean-action gets the same linters on a warm cache.",
      "category": "INSIGHT",
